Z||000009||Pontiaddict||10-28-2001||03:28 AM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jeff3.jpg"> <P>I can explain the picture.<BR>When the NOS was first hit, the 'kart pulled the wheelie. The wheelie bar stopped the rise and the extra power was turned into wheelspin. You really need to rethink your setup? The only thing I can't explain is how he's leaning forward, all that power should have planted him in the seat.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>[Too bad I couldn't find a picture of an exhaust stinger, especially one shooting flames.]||||reg||1
Z||000010||Nashco||10-28-2001||04:09 AM||||Wheelie bar, excellent thinking, and easy to draw!  That's what we call thinking outside the box (I'm still learning <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">).  As for him leaning forward....somebody could try and insert a pillow or something, and say he was leaning forward so he'd have more weight up front.  The first wheelie he did he broke the wheelie bar and had to make another one, so he was trying to not pull such a big wheelie and still spin the tires <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
